## Why This Is Asked
Tests reasoning with partial information in policy constraints using 3-valued semantics, plus constructing a concrete model and a practical propagation approach.

## Key Concepts
- Kleene 3-valued logic semantics for ∧, ∨, ¬, and →
- Evaluate constraints with partial assignments to avoid any F outcomes
- Backtracking and forward propagation tailored to a small constraint set

## Code Example
```javascript
// Lightweight Kleene helpers (conceptual)
const rank = {F:0, U:1, T:2};
const not3 = v => v==='T'?'F': v==='F'?'T':'U';
const min3 = (a,b) => rank[a] <= rank[b] ? a : b;
const max3 = (a,b) => rank[a] >= rank[b] ? a : b;
const imp3 = (a,b) => max3(not3(a), b);
```

